

  How to run it

  # Dry-run (default, no VMs created):
  ./system_validate.sh
  # Actually provision VMs in AWS + Nutanix:
  PROVISION_VMS=1 ./system_validate.sh
  VERBOSE=1 PROVISION_VMS=1 ./system_validate.sh   # surface HTTP bodies
  ONLY=provision PROVISION_VMS=1 ./system_validate.sh

  You can still override individual catalog choices with the same env vars the scripts already accept, e.g. AWS_REGION=..., AWS_INSTANCE_ARCH=arm64,
  IMAGE_ID=..., SIZE_ID=..., SUBNET_ID=..., CLUSTER_ID=..., VM_NAME=....

  Prerequisites for live provisioning (not enforced by the harness)

  • Vault must hold real backend credentials for the aws-prod and ntnx-lab auth_bindings (or whatever LIBCLOUD_AWS_AUTH_BINDING /
    LIBCLOUD_NTNX_AUTH_BINDING resolve to).
  • The REST API's server-side identity must actually be able to reach AWS / Nutanix.
  • For Nutanix: NUTANIX_HOST / NUTANIX_PORT / NUTANIX_API_VERSION / NUTANIX_VERIFY_SSL must point at a real Prism Central.

  One caveat worth flagging

  The harness creates VMs but does not tear them down — the provisioning scripts have no delete path. If you want, I can add a TEARDOWN_VMS=1 option that
  lists /v1/compute/nodes, finds the libcloud-demo-* / libcloud-ntnx-* VMs created this run, and DELETEs them at the end of the provision section. Say the
  word and I'll wire it up.


